<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed flat 2.43 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed flat 2.43 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.1520 to the dollar, down from 3.1425 on Thursday and at 1.8545 to the mark, up from 1.8595, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 2.43 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, unchanged from Thursday's fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
